      "ai": {
        "model": "deepseek-v4.1",
        "v": 11,
        "title": "Cloud connect repo analytics event and experimental model badge field",
        "summary": "The AnalyticsEvent enum in common/src/constants/analytics-events.ts gains FREEBUFF_CLOUD_CONNECT_REPO_CLICKED, which fires when a logged-out visitor clicks a Continue with GitHub or Connect your repo CTA on the Freebuff /cloud landing page and carries a location property to distinguish hero, migration/lovable, and final CTA clicks. Separately, common/src/constants/freebuff-models.ts adds an experimental?: boolean field to the FreebuffModelOption interface and sets experimental: true on the HY3, HY3 Atlas, and KAT Coder Pro V2 model option objects, marking them with a TEST badge in the picker so users know they are still being trialed.",
        "significance": "notable",
        "audience": "maintainers",
        "evidence": "In common/src/constants/analytics-events.ts, the FREEBUFF_CLOUD_CONNECT_REPO_CLICKED enum value (='freebuff.cloud_connect_repo_clicked') is added with a comment describing it as fired on the Freebuff Cloud landing page (/cloud) when a logged-out visitor clicks a Continue with GitHub / Connect your repo CTA; in common/src/constants/freebuff-models.ts, three model option objects (HY3_MODEL, HY3_ATLAS_MODEL, KAT_CODER_PRO_V2_MODEL) gain an experimental: true field, and the FreebuffModelOption interface gains an experimental?: boolean field with a comment stating it is surfaced in the picker as a TEST badge.",
        "userVisible": false,
        "confidence": "high",
        "unknowns": "The diff does not show who emits FREEBUFF_CLOUD_CONNECT_REPO_CLICKED at the /cloud landing page or how the experimental field is consumed by the picker UI to render the TEST badge.",
        "verify": "passed",
